[
  {
    "_comments": [
      "THE VOTING PERMISSION MODEL (docs/voting/security.md). Every voting table except the four catalogs is created with no role",
      "permissions (codegen/additional-schema-info.json, AutoAddPermissions=false). This file is the whole grant list for them.",
      "",
      "UI (every signed-in Explorer user): read only the election CONFIGURATION members need to find and render an election, behind",
      "row-level-security filters (metadata/row-level-security-filters): an election is visible once its roll is frozen, because the",
      "draft may carry an inline CSV roll; comments only on Open ballots; certification records only once certified.",
      "Voting Administrator: runs the administrative operations as themselves, so it holds what those engines touch. No DELETE anywhere.",
      "Election Inspector: reads the audit-relevant tables and co-signs the certification (certification + certifiers + its audit row).",
      "Voting Ballot Engine: held only by the MJ system user. It acts as the system principal for the voter-facing operations, the public",
      "edge, scheduled jobs and any administrative operation run as the system user, so per table it holds AT LEAST what the Voting",
      "Administrator holds, plus the writes only the engines make (poll book create, ballot box). The poll book and audit trail are",
      "create-and-read only; the ballot-box rows are in .entity-permissions.json. Only Ballot Comments can be deleted (a revote replaces",
      "its comments). No role holds DELETE on the poll book, audit trail, roll, credentials, proxies, trustees, results or the ballot box.",
      "Developer and Integration hold nothing here: administering elections is a Voting Administrator grant, not a platform perk.",
      "The four catalogs keep CodeGen's default grants (UI read; Developer and Integration full CRUD, they are seeded metadata); the engine",
      "role also reads them so the system principal never depends on the UI role."
    ],
